// A stream as claude -p sends it to a subscription session near its weekly limit — written by hand for
// `limits/tests.rs` (lines starting `//` are skipped). The shapes are the fields the user's live check L2
// (2026-10-10, its own run outside the project) printed and shared, as target/sb/apibill-design.md §2 "Seen
// live (L2)" records them; where a shape needs more than was shared, the value is made up. Ids are stand-ins.
//
// 1. `system/init` — shape from Claude Code's SDK types (sdk-ts-sdk.d.ts, SDKSystemMessage); `apiKeySource`
//    "none" as L2 printed it. `model`, `claude_code_version`: made up.
// 2. `rate_limit_event` — `rate_limit_info`'s fields as L2 printed them: `status` allowed_warning, `rateLimitType`
//    seven_day, `utilization` 0.92 (a fraction), `surpassedThreshold` 0.75, `isUsingOverage` false. `resetsAt`:
//    made up (L2's wasn't shared) — the same instant as line 3's `resets_at`, in seconds. `unifiedWindows`: L2
//    printed the name only, undeclared in sdk-ts-sdk.d.ts; its contents here are made up.
// 3. The `control_response` to `get_usage` (asked as `u` in L2) — fields as L2 printed them: `subscription_type`
//    max, `rate_limits_available` true, `five_hour` {utilization 0}, `seven_day` {utilization 93 (a percent),
//    resets_at 2026-10-13T01:00Z}, `seven_day_opus` and `seven_day_sonnet` null. `five_hour`'s `resets_at`: made up
//    (null). `seven_day_breakdown`: L2 printed rows of it, undeclared; their contents here are made up.
//    `behaviors` null as `skip_behaviors` makes it (sdk-ts-sdk.d.ts).
// 4. The turn's `result` — shape from the SDK types (SDKResultSuccess); every value made up.
